  "step_2": "The individual considers Lottery A as offering a guaranteed large sum (3000 Euros). They express that it was not worth taking the risk in Lottery B to potentially win a slightly higher amount (4000 Euros), even though the chance is high (80%). The individual emphasizes the certainty of the outcome in A and the perceived unworthiness of the risk in B for a marginal gain. The deliberation focuses on the certainty of a large payout versus the risk of getting nothing, despite the high probability of winning in B. The individual does not mention probabilities below 20%, nor do they refer to any adjustment of probabilities or weighted sums based on probability thresholds. The justification is based on risk aversion and the value of certainty, not on a formal reweighting of low-probability outcomes.",
